# System Security Audit (macOS + Linux)

Two standard audit workflows — choose the right one based on the target.

---

## 1. Local macOS Security Scan

Run when the user asks to "check for suspicious programs" or "security check my Mac."

**Command batch (parallel independent calls) — run in one response round:**

```bash
# 1. Running processes by CPU/memory
ps -eo pid,pcpu,pmem,comm -r | head -30

# 2. Network connections (established + listening)
lsof -i -P -n | awk 'NR==1 || !seen[$1,$9]++' | head -50

# 3. Login items
osascript -e 'tell application "System Events" to get the name of every login item'

# 4. User launch agents (non-Apple)
ls ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v 'com\\.apple' | head -30

# 5. System launch daemons (non-Apple)
ls /Library/LaunchDaemons/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v com.apple | head -20

# 6. System launch agents (non-Apple)
ls /Library/LaunchAgents/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v com.apple | head -20

# 7. MDM / configuration profiles
profiles -C 2>/dev/null

# 8. Installed applications (quick scan for unusual names)
ls /Applications/ | sort

# 9. SSH config and keys
ls -la ~/.ssh/

# 10. Root processes (non-Apple)
ps -U root -o pid,pcpu,pmem,comm -r | grep -v -E '(com\\.apple|kernel_task|launchd)' | head -15

# 11. Listening ports only
lsof -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN -P -n 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR==1 || !/com\\.apple/' | head -25

# 12. Crontabs and at jobs
crontab -l 2>/dev/null; echo "---"; atq 2>/dev/null
```

**What to look for in results:**
- ❌ Unknown network connections to foreign IPs (cryptominers, C2)
- ❌ Non-Apple kernel extensions (`kextstat | grep -v com.apple`)
- ❌ Suspicious Launch Agents/Daemons with nonsensical names
- ❌ Login items the user didn't install
- ❌ Unusual SUID binaries (`find / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null`)
- ❌ SSH authorized_keys entries the user didn't authorize
- ✅ Standard tools: VPN clients (FortiClient, Cato, Pulse), MDM (Intune, Jamf), AV (TrendMicro, Defender, SentinelOne), password managers

**Reporting pattern:**
- Summary verdict first: "✅ Clean" or "⚠️ Issues found"
- Table: check item | status | details
- Priority-ordered action items if issues found

